"Targeting Construct Tasks": {
  "index": "-97",
  "category": "constructs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Targeting Construct Tasks"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "When making construct tasks, you'll often need to tell them what to target, be it a block, a whole range of blocks, or entities (mobs) within an area.\n\nFor a single point, this can be done using a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Rune of Marking",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  To set its location and direction, hold the rune of marking in your hand and "
        },
        {
          "text": "right click on the block you want to mark",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  The arrow shows what side the construct will try to interact with the block from, and is based on the side of the block you clicked on.\n\nFor a range, this can be done in two ways.  The first way is to use two runes of marking and mark the opposite corners of the bounds you wish to use "
        },
        {
          "text": "(remember, you can hold one rune in each hand to visualize the area)",
          "italic": true,
          "color": "dark_gray"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nThe second way is to use a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Marking Rune Pair",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  This allows you to set an area with a single click.  Right clicking on a block with a Marking Rune Pair will "
        },
        {
          "text": "search a 9x9 area centered on the block that was clicked.  The bounding box that will be set will be one containing all blocks that are the same block as the one clicked on within the search area",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  For instance, all wheat blocks, or all chests, all oak logs, etc.  Tags are not searched.\n\nThe area can then be modified by opening the Marking Rune Pair's GUI, allowing you to fine-tune the x/y/z sizes to your liking.  The GUI is opened by holding the M&A GUI hotkey and right clicking with the rune, similar to a Practitioner's Pouch or Spell Book.\n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Marking Rune Pairs, when used on a lodestar parameter that takes 2 marking runes will set both corners of the area.",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "related_recipes": [
